<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">County of Geneva</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">11th century–1401</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Genevois</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The County of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geneva">Geneva</a> was a feudal county in the region around Geneva and Annecy, whose counts held the lands about the city from the eleventh century while the city itself was ruled by its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a>. In 1401 Amadeus VIII of Savoy bought the county, known as the Genevois, from the heir of the last counts, and it became part of the Savoyard state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/county-of-geneva.jpg" alt="County of Geneva" width="320" height="327" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marco Zanoli (Sidonius) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_Kingdom_Arelat_EN.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
